Version: [current]
Command: monochange

monochange discovers packages across Cargo, npm/pnpm/Bun, Deno, and Dart/Flutter, then coordinates version bumps, changelogs, and release automation from a single monochange.toml config.

[1m[97mUsage:[0m [93mmonochange[0m [95m[OPTIONS][0m [95m<COMMAND>[0m

[1m[96mBuilt-in Commands:[0m
  [93msnapshot[0m   Print a normalized JSON snapshot of the CLI surface
  [93minit[0m       Generate monochange.toml with detected packages, groups, and default CLI commands
  [93mpopulate[0m   Add any missing built-in CLI commands to monochange.toml so you can customize them
  [93mcommand[0m    Open an interactive dashboard for adding or editing config-defined CLI commands
  [93mskill[0m      Install the monochange skill bundle into the current project with the skills CLI
  [93msubagents[0m  Generate repo-local monochange subagents and agent guidance files
  [93manalyze[0m    Analyze semantic changes for one package across main, head, and optional release baselines
  [93mmigrate[0m    Audit or migrate release metadata for monochange repositories
  [93mlint[0m       Inspect and scaffold manifest lint rules
  [93mversions[0m   List package and group versions or sync internal dependency constraints
  [93mmcp[0m        Start the monochange MCP (Model Context Protocol) server over stdin/stdout
  [93mcheck[0m      Validate configuration, changesets, and run manifest lint rules
  [93mhelp[0m       Show detailed help for a command
  [93mstep[0m       Run built-in release workflow steps
  [93mrun[0m        Run workflow commands defined in monochange.toml

[1m[96mOptions:[0m
  [93m-h[0m, [93m--help[0m
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  [93m-V[0m, [93m--version[0m
          Print version

[1m[96mGlobal Options:[0m
  [93m-q[0m, [93m--quiet[0m
          Suppress stdout/stderr output and run in dry-run mode when supported

      [93m--progress-format[0m[95m [0m[95m<FORMAT>[0m
          Control progress output on stderr
          
          [possible values: auto, unicode, ascii, json]

      [93m--jq[0m[95m [0m[95m<EXPRESSION>[0m
          Filter JSON output with a jq-style expression, such as `.assets[].name`

      [93m--snapshot[0m
          Print a normalized JSON snapshot for this command subtree

Quick CLI workflow

1. Create or update monochange.toml for your workspace:

  monochange init

2. Validate configuration and changeset targets before making release changes:

  monochange step validate

3. Inspect detected package ids and groups when authoring changesets or workflow inputs:

  monochange step discover --format json

4. Use repository-defined workflows through monochange run <command> when they exist in your config, or call immutable built-in steps directly with monochange step <name>.

5. Preview before mutating files, publishing packages, creating tags, or opening release requests:

  monochange run release --dry-run --diff
  monochange step prepare-release --dry-run --diff

Run monochange help <command> or monochange help step <name> for command-specific options.
